  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="43.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIIIAtr">VIII Atr</ref> 43.1</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="43.1" corresp="#wit-d">⁊ utan God lufian innewerdre heortan ⁊ Godes laga gíman, swa wel swa we betst magon.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">And let us love God from our inmost heart and observe his laws to the best of our ability.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-d">And let us love God with our inmost heart and heed God’s laws as well as ever we can.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und lasst uns Gott aus innerstem Herzen lieben und Gottes Gesetze achten, so gut wie wir bestens können.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let us love God from our inmost hearts and heed God's laws as well as we best can.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VI Atr 1, 42.2.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
